℃ ( 392 F)</td><td id="sjs-D9" data-t="s" data-v="200 C ( 392 F)">200 ℃ ( 392 F)</td><td id="sjs-E9" data-t="s" data-v="200 C ( 392 F)">200 ℃( 392 F)</td></tr><tr><td id="sjs-A10" colspan="2" data-t="s" data-v="Number of plies">Number of plies</td><td id="sjs-C10" data-t="s" data-v="3">3</td><td id="sjs-D10" data-t="s" data-v="5">5</td><td id="sjs-E10" data-t="s" data-v="5">5</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ps: Tolerance of thickness: +/- 0.3mm, gram weight: +/- 5%, air permeability: +/- 10%.</p><h3>Features of Polyester Air Slide Fabric</h3><ul><li>Wear resistance: Polyester air slide fabric is made of polyester fiber, which has excellent wear resistance and can withstand long-term repeated use and material friction, allowing it to maintain stability in high-intensity working environments.</li><li>Corrosion resistance: It has high resistance to a variety of chemicals, so it performs well when used in environments subject to chemical corrosion and is not easily damaged.</li><li>High strength: It has high strength, and the conveyor belt made can withstand large tensile force and is not easy to break or deform, ensuring the stability and safety of the conveying process.</li><li>Low elongation: It has a low elongation, maintains stable dimensions even under high loads, and is not prone to relaxation, ensuring the accuracy and reliability of the conveying system.</li><li>Easy to clean: Its surface is smooth and dirt does not adhere easily, making it easy to clean and maintain, reducing downtime and maintenance costs.</li><li>Economy: It has a lower cost and is more economical than conveyor belts made of other materials.</li></ul><h3>Applications of Polyester Air Slide Fabric:</h3><p>The design of polyester air-slip fabrics usually takes into account the characteristics of the material and the needs of the conveying system, and can be customized into different sizes, structures and surface properties to meet the needs of different industries and applications. They are widely used in production and transportation processes in various fields such as food processing, mining, chemicals, logistics, and construction materials.</p><ul><li><strong>Power Stations</strong>: Filtered dust, flue ash, discharging flue ash, coal dust, etc.</li><li><strong>Building and Construction</strong>: Cement, furnace dust, gypsum, limestone, finely ground quartz, calcium hydroxide, lead monoxide, quicklime, acid crystals, Pure clay, phosphates, magnesite concentrate, finely ground<br />fluorid, production of aluminum, etc.</li><li><strong>Chemical Industry</strong> : Fertilizer, rubber compounds, sinter dust, catalysts, sodium sulfate, soap powder, etc.</li><li><strong>Silos/Tanks</strong>: Discharging systems, warehouse units, mixing equipment, Homogenizing systems.</li><li><strong>Chute Bottoms</strong>: Conveyor systems, ventilator systems, aeration systems.</li><li><strong>Vehicles:</strong> Silo truck discharging cones, railway wagon discharging cones, vessel aeration &amp; discharging bottoms, container aeration &amp; discharging bottoms.</li></ul>						</div>
